{"study_accession":"PRJNA1333682","secondary_study_accession":"SRP626243","title":"Enhanced Trained Immunity in Peripheral Monocytes in Unstable Angina With Elevated High-Sensitivity C-Reactive Protein","description":"Despite effective secondary prevention for coronary heart diseases, recurrent events remain high. Elevated high-sensitivity C-reactive protein (hsCRP) indicates increased inflammation risk. This study aimed to investigate the trained immunity of circulating monocytes in unstable angina (UA) patients with elevated hsCRP. We analyzed CD14-positive monocytes from UA patients, comparing high-risk and low-risk groups. We assessed cytokine production and conducted metabolic, transcriptional, and epigenetic profiling. Patients with elevated hsCRP exhibited enhanced proinflammatory responses, glycolytic activity, and altered immune profiles, indicating sustained monocyte trained immunity, which contributes to residual inflammation risk in cardiovascular disease.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":24,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN51804479","study_accession":"PRJNA1333682","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"L1U","description":"L1U","sex":"male","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-09-28","attributes":[["isolate","LowRisk_1_LPS_Unstimulated"],["age","55"],["biomaterial_provider","Wuhan Union Hospital"],["collection_date","2023-03"],["geo_loc_name","China: Wuhan"],["sex","male"],["tissue","Blood"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR35579288","experiment_accession":"SRX30651986","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"PolyA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":23682091,"base_count":7104627300,"first_public":"2025-09-28","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: RNA-Seq of Homo sapiens: circulating monocyte"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN51804480","study_accession":"PRJNA1333682","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","